Found during k72 (worker), a gap in the k70 bound: check asks backend.check(sourceVersion(oldLock, name)); when nothing from a declared git/url source is in the lock (its only item blocked by a conflict, missing from the source, an empty wildcard over it), the version is undefined and check() reports changed. So every SessionStart syncs and fetches again and repeats the warning, although unreached.json already holds the drift (e.g. missing:skills/foo@src) – contrary to README ("does not count again until a sync runs anyway"). A `local` source syncing every session is by design and out of scope. Repro: git source, its only item conflicts with a hand-written file; sync; `check --json` → sources[src].changed true, exit 1. Fix idea: record the resolved version of every source the last sync read (state or lock, per scope) and let check compare against that when the lock has no entry. Tests: black-box through runHook – the second session after such a sync is silent and fetches nothing.

